    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension of the structure already established in this file.\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** Email validation already lives in `normalizeEmail`, and the controller already carries validation data as private static constants (`EMAIL_PATTERN`, `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS`). Adding `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` as a sibling constant and extending `normalizeEmail` places the new rule exactly where the existing email rule lives \u2014 the natural spot a maintainer would look.\n- **No duplication.** The blocklist is a single source of truth, and the domain check reuses the already-computed `normalized` value rather than re-lowercasing.\n- **Not a catch-all.** `normalizeEmail` remains narrowly about validating/normalizing one field; the addition is one cohesive concern (domain acceptability), not unrelated responsibilities piling onto the method.\n- **Idiomatic.** `Set.of(...)`, `Locale.ROOT` lower-casing, and reusing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"email\"))` match the surrounding style and the existing 400 path. The Javadoc was updated to match, keeping docs coherent with behavior.",
